        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7a2bd107-99a9-5f72-b635-e4212fa04225",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jon Heder, Jeremy Coon, Rob Schneider, David Spade, Patrick Stewart, James Roday, Julianna Guill, Cheryl Hines, Gary Cole, Roy Disney\n- Films and Series: Napoleon Dynamite, The Benchwarmers, School for Scoundrels, Blades of Glory, Mama's Boy, When in Rome, Walt Before Mickey, Monster House, Surf's Up, Christmas Eve, Napoleon Dynamite animated series\n- Companies: Revolution Studios, Happy Madison Productions, Columbia Pictures\n- Roles: actor, producer, executive producer, editor\n\nFacts:\n- Jon Heder was born on October 26, 1977, and he is an American actor and producer.\n- Jeremy Coon was born in 1979, and he is an American executive producer and editor.\n- Jon Heder made his feature film debut in 2004 by playing the title character in Napoleon Dynamite.\n- Jeremy Coon was the executive producer and editor of the 2004 film Napoleon Dynamite.\n- Napoleon Dynamite was made on a $400,000 budget and earned more than $44 million after its release.\n- Jon Heder starred in The Benchwarmers with Rob Schneider and David Spade.\n- The Benchwarmers was produced by Revolution Studios and Happy Madison Productions and distributed by Columbia Pictures.\n- Jon Heder also acted in School for Scoundrels, Blades of Glory, Mama's Boy, When in Rome, and Walt Before Mickey, in which he played Roy Disney.\n- Jon Heder provided voice acting for Monster House, Surf's Up, and the Napoleon Dynamite animated series.\n- The 2015 film Christmas Eve features an ensemble cast led by Patrick Stewart, James Roday, Julianna Guill, Jon Heder, Cheryl Hines, and Gary Cole.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6dbd52f3-7d89-5c2c-997e-b8e9fcef84b5",
        "text": "Page: Jon Heder. Sentence: Jonathan Joseph \"Jon\" Heder ( ) (born October 26, 1977) is an American actor and producer.\nPage: Jon Heder. Sentence: His feature film debut came in 2004 as the title character of the comedy film \"Napoleon Dynamite\".\nPage: Jon Heder. Sentence: He has also acted in the films \"The Benchwarmers\", \"School for Scoundrels\", \"Blades of Glory\", \"Mama's Boy\", \"When in Rome\", and \"Walt Before Mickey\" as Roy Disney, and provided voice talents in the animated films \"Monster House\" and \"Surf's Up\", as well as the \"Napoleon Dynamite\" animated series.\nPage: The Benchwarmers. Sentence: It stars Rob Schneider, David Spade, and Jon Heder.\nPage: The Benchwarmers. Sentence: It is produced by Revolution Studios and Happy Madison Productions and is distributed by Columbia Pictures.\nPage: Christmas Eve (2015 film). Sentence: The film features a large ensemble cast led by Patrick Stewart, James Roday, Julianna Guill, Jon Heder, Cheryl Hines, and Gary Cole.\nPage: Jeremy Coon. Sentence: Jeremy Coon (born 1979) is an American executive producer and editor of the 2004 film \"Napoleon Dynamite\", a cult hit made on a $400,000 budget that has earned more than $44 million since its release.",
